WEBVTT

00:10.190 --> 00:10.240
Natsume's Book of Friends 6

00:15.990 --> 00:19.990
Things I want are beyond my reach

00:19.990 --> 00:23.970
Wishes I pray for won't ever come true

00:23.970 --> 00:31.330
I hate myself for having these depressing and envious thoughts

00:31.840 --> 00:35.780
But I'm not alone in being like that

00:35.780 --> 00:39.780
And I believe that there's a bud

00:39.780 --> 00:47.310
That won't turn into a beautiful flower unless I make it bloom

00:49.030 --> 00:57.560
I'll accept all the regrets and worries that I've had until now

00:57.560 --> 00:59.600
And water the bud in my heart

00:59.600 --> 01:05.460
I'm sure there's a meaning to all the tears I've shed

01:05.460 --> 01:09.450
I've always been searching for what was born from them

01:09.450 --> 01:13.410
And realized it's always been right here

01:13.410 --> 01:17.420
If only I can love myself the way I am

01:17.420 --> 01:21.220
It'll become my own beautiful flower

01:21.220 --> 01:28.560
I won't hesitate anymore and make it bloom

01:33.010 --> 01:37.510
97. 98. 99.

01:38.340 --> 01:39.200
100.

01:40.280 --> 01:43.220
101. 102.

01:44.040 --> 01:45.360
103.

01:48.920 --> 01:51.790
One, two, three.

01:53.700 --> 01:55.690
Hey, isn't that Tamami?

01:55.690 --> 01:56.920
You're right.

01:56.920 --> 01:59.680
She's up to something again.

01:59.680 --> 02:01.640
28, 29...

02:00.320 --> 02:02.090
Tamami!

02:02.090 --> 02:03.930
What are you doing?

02:07.220 --> 02:08.690
Nothing important!

02:12.140 --> 02:15.110
Go home before it gets too late!

02:15.110 --> 02:16.100
Bye!

02:16.100 --> 02:17.610
Got it!

02:17.610 --> 02:18.890
Bye!

02:22.210 --> 02:24.130
Guess I'll have to start over.

02:26.340 --> 02:30.210
38, 39, 40.

02:30.800 --> 02:34.710
41, 42, 43.

02:35.140 --> 02:39.420
61, 62, 63.

02:47.070 --> 02:48.240
Turn south.

02:48.240 --> 02:51.280
One, two, three.

03:00.740 --> 03:04.740
A Fragment of a Phantasm

03:13.430 --> 03:14.440
Oh no!

03:14.440 --> 03:17.760
I fell asleep eating my lunch!

03:22.160 --> 03:27.110
If my friends saw me like this,
I'm sure they'd laugh at me again.

03:31.360 --> 03:33.100
<i>It's because of that dream I had.</i>

03:33.100 --> 03:34.480
<i>I'm a little behind on sleep.</i>

03:35.420 --> 03:37.330
I'm sure of it. This way.

03:39.060 --> 03:39.930
I knew it.

03:39.930 --> 03:42.140
Right on the other side of these bushes!

03:43.100 --> 03:44.660
<i>Somebody's coming.</i>

03:45.340 --> 03:46.910
But why?

03:47.250 --> 03:49.250
Why do I smell...

03:49.250 --> 03:51.840
fried shrimp here in the forest?

03:55.520 --> 03:57.990
A-A-A talking cat!

03:57.990 --> 03:59.040
<i>Oops!</i>

03:59.040 --> 04:01.800
<i>She heard me so clearly that there's no getting out of this!</i>

04:02.380 --> 04:04.720
Th-This is impossible.

04:04.720 --> 04:07.480
Am I dreaming again?

04:07.480 --> 04:08.810
Yeah, that's it!

04:08.810 --> 04:11.240
You're dreaming.

04:11.240 --> 04:12.740
Why is a cat talking?

04:12.740 --> 04:14.770
Is that even a cat?

04:14.770 --> 04:18.660
I'm definitely a cute, little cat!

04:18.660 --> 04:22.320
Calm down, me! Calm down, calm down!

04:22.320 --> 04:24.330
Calm down!

04:26.050 --> 04:28.080
Have you calmed down, girl?

04:29.130 --> 04:30.870
Y-Yes...

04:31.930 --> 04:32.800
Listen.

04:32.800 --> 04:34.420
This is a dream.

04:34.420 --> 04:39.460
So there's nothing odd about a talking cat.

04:40.060 --> 04:41.760
I see!

04:41.760 --> 04:43.570
I'm glad you understand.

04:47.220 --> 04:48.940
<i>This feeling...</i>

04:48.940 --> 04:51.720
It's like Alice in Wonderland!

04:51.720 --> 04:53.340
Ice? Ice cream?

04:53.340 --> 04:54.290
Alice!

04:54.290 --> 04:55.940
Alice?

04:55.940 --> 04:57.900
Can you eat that?

04:57.900 --> 04:59.420
You're a silly kitty.

04:59.420 --> 05:00.860
It's Master Nyanko!

05:00.860 --> 05:02.490
Master?

05:04.670 --> 05:06.140
That was so good.

05:06.140 --> 05:07.740
Thank you.

05:08.210 --> 05:09.950
You're welcome.

05:09.950 --> 05:13.000
So what are you doing here, Master Nyanko?

05:14.020 --> 05:15.980
I'm a great demon, you see?

05:15.980 --> 05:19.780
And I have a human boy as a servant.

05:19.780 --> 05:21.260
<i>That escalated quickly...</i>

05:21.260 --> 05:27.300
But he's so wimpy and frail,
has a mean look, and always runs off.

05:27.300 --> 05:28.930
Have you seen him?

05:28.930 --> 05:29.880
No.

05:29.880 --> 05:30.890
I see.

05:31.170 --> 05:33.390
Anyway, what are you doing here?

05:35.570 --> 05:36.780
Well...

05:39.880 --> 05:40.760
Over there!

05:40.760 --> 05:43.690
Wh-What was that scream?

05:43.690 --> 05:45.280
Bye, girl!

05:46.170 --> 05:48.140
This isn't a normal forest.

05:48.140 --> 05:49.630
Go home, now.

05:50.280 --> 05:51.650
Master Nyanko!

05:57.690 --> 05:58.740
Wait!

06:01.690 --> 06:03.550
Where are you, Master Nyanko?

06:24.940 --> 06:27.940
Did I just imagine it?

06:30.150 --> 06:32.790
<i>I guess this really isn't a normal forest.</i>

06:39.770 --> 06:41.030
<i>Calm down.</i>

06:41.030 --> 06:42.350
<i>Don't get scared.</i>

06:43.580 --> 06:45.530
<i>I have something I need to do.</i>

06:50.740 --> 06:52.020
<i>Somebody's there!</i>

06:52.020 --> 06:52.970
Excuse me!

06:53.290 --> 06:54.470
Um...

06:56.470 --> 07:00.230
Um, I want to ask about this forest.

07:00.640 --> 07:01.900
Stop! Don't get any closer!

07:03.190 --> 07:04.010
Um...

07:04.010 --> 07:05.110
I'm sorry.

07:06.120 --> 07:08.110
You're... human?

07:08.110 --> 07:08.950
Huh?

07:08.950 --> 07:10.040
Of course.

07:10.040 --> 07:12.230
What's a human doing here?

07:12.230 --> 07:13.620
Um, uh...

07:14.000 --> 07:15.870
You're human too, right?

07:15.870 --> 07:19.380
You're still here, girl?

07:19.870 --> 07:21.270
Master Nyanko!

07:21.270 --> 07:22.000
Wh—

07:22.120 --> 07:24.530
Why are you talking around her, Master?

07:24.530 --> 07:27.740
She seems to think it's a dream.

07:27.740 --> 07:29.310
It'll work out.

07:29.310 --> 07:31.630
Don't pinch the kitty!

07:33.460 --> 07:35.390
What if it doesn't work out?

07:35.950 --> 07:37.360
Don't worry.

07:37.360 --> 07:40.140
When she does leave this forest...

07:40.140 --> 07:40.820
Huh?

07:40.820 --> 07:44.070
Well, it's not your problem.

07:44.070 --> 07:45.180
Um...

07:45.900 --> 07:47.850
Sorry for startling you.

07:47.850 --> 07:50.730
I was following the kit—Master Nyanko,

07:50.730 --> 07:54.660
and I thought I saw something
weird that looked like a monster.

07:55.370 --> 07:56.950
I got scared and...

07:56.950 --> 07:58.130
Huh? You saw it?

07:58.130 --> 07:59.160
Yes.

08:00.540 --> 08:03.150
This forest is its own little world.

08:03.150 --> 08:07.390
There may be moments when you
can see things you normally couldn't.

08:07.390 --> 08:08.440
Master...

08:08.440 --> 08:10.170
Is there really something here?

08:10.170 --> 08:15.190
This is called the Forest of the Gospel,
and it's ruled by a divine protector-class of spirits.

08:15.190 --> 08:17.930
Don't worry. Nobody here is that weird.

08:17.930 --> 08:19.530
Nobody?

08:19.530 --> 08:21.480
I was almost attacked.

08:21.480 --> 08:23.410
You're special.

08:24.890 --> 08:28.890
I don't understand, but this place is amazing.

08:29.550 --> 08:31.070
I'll take you to the exit.

08:31.070 --> 08:31.840
What?

08:31.840 --> 08:34.690
You shouldn't stay too long in a place you don't understand.

08:34.690 --> 08:35.390
Let's go.

08:36.110 --> 08:38.830
I-I'm sorry,

08:39.510 --> 08:40.910
but I can't go back yet.

08:40.910 --> 08:41.740
Huh?

08:41.740 --> 08:45.340
Did you see a white owl in this forest?

08:45.340 --> 08:48.590
A white owl asked me to come here.

08:50.090 --> 08:51.590
An owl asked you to come?

08:51.590 --> 08:57.100
Oh, um... Sorry for saying something so absurd.

08:57.100 --> 08:59.070
No, I'm curious.

08:59.070 --> 08:59.850
Huh?

08:59.850 --> 09:02.350
Can you tell me more?

09:02.350 --> 09:04.680
No. You'll just laugh at me.

09:04.680 --> 09:05.670
I won't.

09:06.790 --> 09:07.820
I promise.

09:12.210 --> 09:14.500
It started a few days ago...

09:15.970 --> 09:20.130
On the way home from school,
as I was walking under a big tree...

09:27.080 --> 09:29.280
You said you wouldn't laugh!

09:29.280 --> 09:30.670
I'm not laughing.

09:30.670 --> 09:32.760
I just don't get what's going on.

09:32.760 --> 09:39.090
Basically, there was a white owl tangled up in a fishing line and hanging from a branch.

09:39.090 --> 09:41.600
I thought I should help it, so...

09:44.020 --> 09:45.720
Ow...

09:47.520 --> 09:49.390
J-Just wait, okay?

09:51.650 --> 09:54.080
I managed to get the line off the branch.

09:54.650 --> 09:56.200
Whew...

09:57.400 --> 09:58.610
Just wait.

09:58.610 --> 10:00.420
I'll get it off your leg.

10:02.660 --> 10:05.370
This is what it got tangled on, huh?

10:11.050 --> 10:12.120
Got it!

10:12.120 --> 10:13.510
That's good.

10:14.510 --> 10:17.070
Now there's the wound on your forehead.

10:17.070 --> 10:18.180
What do I do?

10:18.670 --> 10:20.070
There's no vet near...

10:26.770 --> 10:27.810
Can you fly?

10:29.810 --> 10:30.460
Huh?

10:42.150 --> 10:43.960
This is the ring.

10:43.960 --> 10:46.360
The owl flew off before I could attach it again.

10:47.510 --> 10:54.370
It's got this pretty red stone on it,
so I kept it so I could give it back if I saw the owl again.

10:54.370 --> 10:56.090
And then last night...

11:04.210 --> 11:05.730
<i>It's the owl.</i>

11:05.730 --> 11:07.190
<i>It's saying something.</i>

11:08.730 --> 11:11.250
A hundred and three steps to the west from that tree.

11:11.250 --> 11:12.950
Forty to the north.

11:12.950 --> 11:15.060
Sixty-three to the east.

11:15.060 --> 11:17.850
Clap your hands in prayer,
then take three steps to the south.

11:17.850 --> 11:20.850
When you turn around, you will find the entrance.

11:22.420 --> 11:24.580
I live in that forest.

11:25.250 --> 11:27.120
I cannot leave for a while.

11:28.210 --> 11:30.430
Please come to return my stone.

11:39.660 --> 11:42.640
I know it was just a dream,

11:42.640 --> 11:46.670
but when I think about how the owl might be in trouble because of me...

11:47.640 --> 11:54.790
So today I brought the ring, made a lunch, did what it said, and came here.

11:54.790 --> 11:55.910
I see.

11:56.810 --> 11:57.980
Where's the owl?

11:57.980 --> 12:01.060
I looked, but I can't find it.

12:01.060 --> 12:04.410
So I took a break, and that's when I met Master Nyanko.

12:04.690 --> 12:07.170
Those fried shrimp were delicious.

12:07.170 --> 12:07.820
Huh?

12:07.820 --> 12:09.850
Were those from your lunch?

12:12.920 --> 12:16.170
I have to give this back, so...

12:18.500 --> 12:21.200
I'll look for the ruler of this forest.

12:21.200 --> 12:23.620
I'll help you find the owl while I'm at it.

12:23.620 --> 12:24.120
Huh?!

12:24.120 --> 12:24.930
You what?!

12:24.930 --> 12:25.920
Thank you!

12:25.920 --> 12:27.860
Um, I'm Tamami!

12:27.860 --> 12:29.180
What's your name?

12:30.510 --> 12:31.680
I'm...

12:33.550 --> 12:34.500
Sorry.

12:34.500 --> 12:35.810
I won't say.

12:36.820 --> 12:41.010
If we meet again in the future,
it'd be bad if you knew my name.

12:42.760 --> 12:44.570
Will we meet again?

12:45.230 --> 12:47.460
I'll ask you again if we do.

12:48.600 --> 12:49.470
Okay.

12:49.470 --> 12:50.840
Let's go look.

12:51.470 --> 12:56.510
Jeez, you're buying me one of those new bean-jam dumplings from Nanatsujiya when we get back.

12:58.400 --> 13:00.440
Hey, their new bean-jam dumpling!

13:00.440 --> 13:02.370
C'mon! Answer me!

13:04.050 --> 13:07.060
Natsume's Book of Friends 6

13:15.170 --> 13:17.440
<i>He was a strange boy.</i>

13:18.130 --> 13:20.940
<i>He talked to trees with nothing on them.</i>

13:18.130 --> 13:19.150
I see.

13:19.880 --> 13:20.940
Thank you.

13:22.830 --> 13:26.070
<i>He looked up at the sky and nodded.</i>

13:30.790 --> 13:34.200
<i>He suddenly grabbed my hand and started running.</i>

13:36.790 --> 13:38.850
<i>Everything he did was strange.</i>

13:47.660 --> 13:49.710
<i>But it was fun and exciting!</i>

13:51.120 --> 13:53.590
<i>It was like...</i>

13:54.970 --> 13:57.620
<i>I was Alice in Wonderland!</i>

14:01.440 --> 14:02.710
I'm tired.

14:04.010 --> 14:04.610
Look.

14:04.990 --> 14:06.040
Over there.

14:06.040 --> 14:06.710
Huh?

14:06.710 --> 14:09.270
In the gap between the roots of that big tree.

14:11.730 --> 14:13.000
Sorry.

14:13.000 --> 14:16.000
I found what I'm looking for first.

14:16.000 --> 14:16.990
Huh?

14:16.990 --> 14:18.500
I'll be right back.

14:18.930 --> 14:20.280
Isn't that great?

14:20.280 --> 14:21.140
Got it.

14:21.140 --> 14:22.000
Good luck.

14:36.640 --> 14:37.520
It's so pretty.

14:42.070 --> 14:43.400
Reiko's grandson?

14:43.710 --> 14:44.690
Yes.

14:44.690 --> 14:48.160
I heard that the entrance to this forest,
which is usually closed, had finally opened,

14:48.160 --> 14:50.320
so I came to return your name.

14:50.320 --> 14:52.410
Thank you for coming.

14:53.170 --> 14:55.660
I'm sorry for binding your name for so long.

14:57.910 --> 15:01.430
You who protect me, show me your name.

15:03.210 --> 15:04.100
Hakuhi.

15:06.530 --> 15:07.600
Please accept this.

15:44.760 --> 15:46.790
It feels good, huh?

15:46.790 --> 15:48.010
Truly.

15:48.880 --> 15:50.470
I knew it.

15:50.470 --> 15:52.380
You're no ordinary owl.

15:54.050 --> 15:55.410
How could you tell?

15:56.040 --> 16:01.350
No owl carries something like that on their ankle in the human world.

16:02.410 --> 16:03.860
Let me guess.

16:04.600 --> 16:07.770
If you're an owl, does that make you the protector of a forest?

16:10.200 --> 16:12.580
Something like that.

16:12.580 --> 16:13.510
Knew it.

16:14.510 --> 16:18.230
What's an amazing demon like you doing in a place like this?

16:18.230 --> 16:23.670
Sometimes I go to purify myself in the lakes on the spirit mountain in order to remove the evil aura of the forest.

16:25.770 --> 16:28.300
Hey, you don't have to head back immediately, right?

16:28.930 --> 16:30.410
Want to play a game with me?

16:33.660 --> 16:35.580
You are lonely too, are you not?

16:36.510 --> 16:40.680
When you are alone for so long, you want to talk to someone.

16:43.630 --> 16:45.580
Here we go...

16:47.770 --> 16:49.690
A white owl?

16:50.080 --> 16:51.060
Yes.

16:51.060 --> 16:55.190
When I leave the forest, I take the avatar of a white owl.

16:55.190 --> 16:56.940
That wound...

16:56.940 --> 17:00.600
Are you the owl who summoned a girl into this forest?

17:00.600 --> 17:02.200
How do you know about that?

17:02.760 --> 17:05.800
She came to this forest to return the stone.

17:06.600 --> 17:08.040
Really?

17:08.040 --> 17:09.210
That is great.

17:10.330 --> 17:11.840
Are you sure about this?

17:11.840 --> 17:18.100
If a spirit starts talking to a normal girl in her dreams, showing itself to her, and calling her places,

17:18.530 --> 17:22.620
and she tells somebody,
the people around her will think she's strange.

17:22.620 --> 17:24.600
It is fine.

17:25.550 --> 17:27.530
As long as I have the stone, it is fine.

17:27.530 --> 17:28.110
Huh?

17:28.780 --> 17:35.930
I have the power to erase her memories of saving me in my owl form

17:36.620 --> 17:41.870
and of coming to the forest where
those who live in the shadows dwell.

17:42.360 --> 17:45.870
You need not worry, grandson of Reiko.

17:47.440 --> 17:49.880
That means...

17:50.170 --> 17:51.210
You'll erase her memories?

17:54.130 --> 17:55.820
Please don't!

17:55.820 --> 17:59.640
You can't steal even a single second
from someone without their permission!

17:59.640 --> 18:06.550
She came here to give it back to you because she wanted to help you!

18:11.550 --> 18:13.400
As the guardian of the forest,

18:13.890 --> 18:15.990
anyone who sees me,

18:15.990 --> 18:20.720
except for priests or priestesses—
or those like you who can see spirits—

18:20.720 --> 18:24.160
must forget or not be allowed to return alive.

18:25.650 --> 18:27.090
Allowed to return alive?

18:28.030 --> 18:30.150
This was my own failure.

18:31.160 --> 18:37.500
I cannot leave the forest now,
so I asked her to bring the stone here to me.

18:38.400 --> 18:41.420
I will erase her memories and send her back.

18:42.530 --> 18:44.930
It is the best exception I can make.

18:44.930 --> 18:45.520
But—

18:45.520 --> 18:49.190
Some laws can't be broken, Natsume.

18:56.510 --> 18:58.760
I must take that stone.

18:58.760 --> 19:00.640
Please lead me there.

19:01.950 --> 19:04.150
My eyes are not that good.

19:05.620 --> 19:08.050
When I flew in the world of men for the first time in ages,

19:08.740 --> 19:11.140
it was filled with new shapes and colors.

19:11.770 --> 19:14.420
It must have blinded me.

19:15.560 --> 19:17.100
I failed.

19:17.970 --> 19:19.370
I failed greatly.

19:26.100 --> 19:27.840
Welcome... back.

19:28.660 --> 19:29.350
The owl!

19:31.230 --> 19:32.100
Thank you!

19:32.100 --> 19:33.760
You found it for me?

19:35.510 --> 19:37.480
I'm so glad I met you again.

19:37.900 --> 19:39.010
It's like a dream!

19:40.000 --> 19:41.720
Is your wound okay?

19:41.720 --> 19:42.690
I'm sorry.

19:42.690 --> 19:44.620
I brought your ring.

19:45.390 --> 19:46.120
Here.

19:49.990 --> 19:51.690
Stick your leg out.

19:52.370 --> 19:54.230
I'll put it on.

20:08.160 --> 20:10.690
Can I take this fragment?

20:18.290 --> 20:19.420
I'll treasure it.

20:20.210 --> 20:21.530
Thank you.

20:24.530 --> 20:26.700
See you later.

20:26.700 --> 20:27.860
I'm sure we'll meet—

20:39.020 --> 20:42.130
It is a shame to be forgotten.

20:45.220 --> 20:50.220
<i>It was a voice I thought I knew, but I didn't.</i>

20:52.100 --> 20:53.320
<i>What was that?</i>

20:53.970 --> 20:58.350
<i>It was such a wonderful dream.</i>

21:09.610 --> 21:10.530
Oh no!

21:10.530 --> 21:11.620
What happened?!

21:12.450 --> 21:16.370
I was sleeping on a park bench?

21:27.390 --> 21:28.760
Goodbye.

21:30.220 --> 21:31.520
Goodbye.

21:36.520 --> 21:38.290
<i>What was that?</i>

21:38.290 --> 21:40.520
<i>It was warm and fuzzy.</i>

21:41.160 --> 21:43.780
<i>Like I was dreaming.</i>

21:47.530 --> 21:48.600
A stone?

21:54.880 --> 21:55.990
It's pretty.

21:59.910 --> 22:01.390
It's so pretty, isn't it?

22:06.490 --> 22:12.630
While I was waiting for the dawn to come

22:12.630 --> 22:18.250
I softly closed my eyes in complete silence

22:18.250 --> 22:24.720
But instead of a new wind I wanted to feel across my skin

22:24.720 --> 22:30.620
A ray of light shined into my heart

22:30.620 --> 22:36.980
Goodnight, my beloved first star

22:36.980 --> 22:43.650
I've been waiting for your radiance

22:43.650 --> 22:49.260
I won't ask you to grant my wishes

22:49.260 --> 22:57.530
Knowing that you're watching over me is enough

22:58.640 --> 23:04.480
You don't need to answer, but I want you to listen

23:04.480 --> 23:10.840
It's not a farewell, but these are my last words

23:10.840 --> 23:23.590
